  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-defense art direction, disciplined cyan/magenta accents, confident headline typography, and clear primary hierarchy across viewports. However, desktop polish is materially weakened by visibly clipped left-column content and an awkwardly cropped code panel; the oversized ghost word behind the desktop header also reads as accidental interference. Tablet/mobile preserve the structure well, but dense microtype, low-contrast secondary labels, a very long card, and horizontally clipped code make the lower half feel cramped and unfinished.",
